diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..7d93b4c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,29 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+Article search loads the pinned Fuse.js 7.1.0 standalone library on demand through
+`src/utils/loadAsset.ts`. The Vite plugin in `build/shared-assets.mjs` hashes the
+package's exact published bytes with SHA-256 at build time and emits those same
+bytes under the app's base URL. No asset download is needed to compute a hash in
+the browser. Upgrading Fuse requires updating the dependency and the asset filename.
+
+The loader first checks Cross-Origin Storage when supported, then fetches from
+the app on any miss or read failure. Permission denials skip write-back; other
+misses attempt a complete write and close. Fuse uses `origins: '*'` because it is
+a widely distributed, public MIT-licensed library. That scope does not guarantee
+availability: popularity and privacy gating can still produce `NotFoundError`.
+Site-specific assets should omit the scope, and assets shared with a small trusted
+set may use explicit origins. Multiple assets use individual concurrent requests.
+
+The library is imported from a temporary JavaScript blob URL, which is revoked
+after import. Deployments with a Content Security Policy must allow `blob:` in
+`script-src` to enable fuzzy search; basic title/summary matching remains available
+if the library cannot load. COS is optional and needs no permission-policy change
+for the top-level site. An embedding site can deny it; normal fetching still works.
+
+Run `npm test` for cache hit, fallback, permissions, full writes, failure, concurrency,
+and build-time hash checks. Run `npm run build` for the production build.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
